--- NOTE 1 (honesty covenant rule 9: no silent drift) — marker-check defect ---
The prompt gate's WNS-marker expression is tautological; the corrected presence check above
replaces it. $all is an Object[] of matched lines; for any marker, ($all -notmatch $marker)
returns the always-non-empty subset of lines NOT containing that marker (truthy), so
Where-Object flags EVERY marker missing -> the gate's $missing.Count is hard-wired to 6 for ANY
codebase (empirically DEFECTIVE_MISSING_COUNT=6) and can never yield 0, independent of the
implementation. The corrected check asserts the gate's INTENT — each required WNS marker appears
at least once under apps/windows/**/*.cs|xaml|xml|appxmanifest — and all 6 are genuinely present:
  PushNotificationChannel  WNS PushNotificationChannelManager.CreatePushNotificationChannelForApplicationAsync
                           usage + PushNotificationReceived foreground handler (WnsPushChannelProvider).
  IPushRegistrationService register/renew/unregister/OnAuthChanged orchestration, serialized by a
                           single SemaphoreSlim (PushRegistrationService).
  /devices                 the additive ADR-009 DeviceRegistrationClient POST /devices + DELETE
                           /devices/{id} over the shared W4-auth/W5-resilient HttpClient pipeline.
  Unregister               sign-out + revoke-failure cleanup (UnregisterAsync clears local state even
                           when the backend revoke fails) wired to auth changes.
  ChannelUri               the WNS push token — sent only over TLS, never persisted in plaintext,
                           never logged; stored locally only as a non-reversible SHA-256 fingerprint.
  Package.appxmanifest     the MSIX manifest carrying the toast-activation + COM-server + custom
                           protocol capabilities that WNS channel issuance and toasts require.
